{title: Let It Be Me}
{artist: Dave Simpfendorfer}
{key: E}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 90}

Verse 1
Who’ll bring the happy news?
Their warfare is now ended
And their debt of sin is fully paid
Who’ll bring the happy news?

Verse 2
Whose voice is calling out?
Prepare the way, now, for the Lord!
Make straight the highway for our God
Whose voice is calling out?

Chorus
Let it be me
Let it be me, my Lord
Let it be me
Let it be me, my Lord

Verse 3
And who’ll prepare His way?
To raise up every valley and
Make crooked straight and rough place smooth
And who’ll prepare His way?

Chorus
Let it be me
Let it be me, my Lord
Let it be me
Let it be me, my Lord
Let it be me
Let it be me, my Lord
Let it be me
Let it be me, my Lord

Bridge
May the Glory of the Lord be revealed
May the Glory of the Lord be revealed 
May the Glory of the Lord 
Be made known in all my life
May His will be ever done
For God has spoken
May the Glory of the Lord be revealed
May the Glory of the Lord be revealed 
May the Glory of the Lord 
Be made known in all my life
For the Word of the Lord
Endures forever

Verse 4
Who’ll shout it from on high?
Who’ll lift their voice up clear and loud?
And say, “Here comes our mighty God!”
Who’ll shout it from on high?

Chorus
Let it be me
Let it be me, my Lord
